{
  "title": "Drums and rhythm",
  "startSide": "back",
  "learned": [
    "A mixer adds signals: melody and drums together",
    "RESET keeps sequencers in step",
    "Triggers play drums",
    "Euclidean rhythms: steps, hits, rotate",
    "Logic: AND of two rhythms",
    "Shaping the kit and swing"
  ],
  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "The melody from lesson 4 is playing. Drums are played by triggers: short pulses that say 'hit now'. A Euclidean sequencer spreads a number of hits as evenly as it can over a number of steps, which is how many rhythms of the world are built.",
      "done": {
        "next": true
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Patch X4 of the clock to CLOCK of the Euclidean sequencer. It now steps on every sixteenth note.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Clock",
          "output": "x4"
        },
        {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "input": "Clock"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "cable": {
          "from": {
            "module": "Clock",
            "output": "x4"
          },
          "to": {
            "module": "Euclid",
            "input": "Clock"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Patch GATE 1 of the Euclidean sequencer to KICK TRIG of the drums.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "output": "Gate 1"
        },
        {
          "module": "Drums",
          "input": "Kick trig"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "cable": {
          "from": {
            "module": "Euclid",
            "output": "Gate 1"
          },
          "to": {
            "module": "Drums",
            "input": "Kick trig"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "To hear the melody and the drums together you need a mixer: it adds signals. Patch OUT 1 of the amplifier to IN 1 of the mixer, MIX of the drums to IN 2, and MIX of the mixer to jack 1 of the patchbay (the old cable goes).",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "VCA",
          "output": "Out 1"
        },
        {
          "module": "Mixer",
          "input": "In 1"
        },
        {
          "module": "Drums",
          "output": "Mix"
        },
        {
          "module": "Mixer",
          "input": "In 2"
        },
        {
          "module": "Mixer",
          "output": "Mix"
        },
        {
          "module": "Patchbay4",
          "input": "Ch 1",
          "side": "back"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "VCA",
                "output": "Out 1"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Mixer",
                "input": "In 1"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Drums",
                "output": "Mix"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Mixer",
                "input": "In 2"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Mixer",
                "output": "Mix"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Patchbay4",
                "input": "Ch 1",
                "side": "back"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "signal": {
              "module": "HostAudio2",
              "input": "#1"
            },
            "above": 0.05
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and turn LEVEL 2 of the mixer until the drums and the melody sit well together. Balancing levels is most of what mixing is.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Mixer",
          "param": "Channel 2 level"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "Mixer",
          "param": "Channel 2 level"
        },
        "moved": 0.15
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Hear how the drums don't sit with the melody? The two sequencers started counting at different moments, so their step 1 is in different places. A reset fixes that: press Tab and patch RESET of the clock to RESET of the Euclidean sequencer and to RESET of the sequencer.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Clock",
          "output": "Reset"
        },
        {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "input": "Reset"
        },
        {
          "module": "SEQ",
          "input": "Reset"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Clock",
                "output": "Reset"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Euclid",
                "input": "Reset"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Clock",
                "output": "Reset"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "SEQ",
                "input": "Reset"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "The clock sends a reset when it starts. Press Tab and flip the clock's switch down to STOP.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Clock",
          "param": "Mode"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "Clock",
          "param": "Mode"
        },
        "max": 0
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Now flip it back up to RUN: both sequencers jump to step 1 together, and the drums and the melody start on the same beat.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Clock",
          "param": "Mode"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "Clock",
          "param": "Mode"
        },
        "min": 2
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn HITS of track 1. Three hits in sixteen steps is a classic off-kilter groove; go back to four for the steady beat.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "param": "Track 1 hits"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "param": "Track 1 hits"
        },
        "moved": 0.06
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and patch GATE 2 to SNARE TRIG and GATE 3 to HAT TRIG of the drums.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "output": "Gate 2"
        },
        {
          "module": "Drums",
          "input": "Snare trig"
        },
        {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "output": "Gate 3"
        },
        {
          "module": "Drums",
          "input": "Hat trig"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Euclid",
                "output": "Gate 2"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Drums",
                "input": "Snare trig"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Euclid",
                "output": "Gate 3"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Drums",
                "input": "Hat trig"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and turn ROTATE of track 2. Rotate shifts the whole pattern later in time without changing it: find the spot where the snare sits on the backbeat.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "param": "Track 2 rotate"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "param": "Track 2 rotate"
        },
        "moved": 0.06
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A logic module combines gates: AND is high only while both inputs are. Press Tab, patch GATE 1 to A and GATE 2 to B of the logic module, and AND to CLAP TRIG of the drums: a clap only where kick and snare meet, on 2 and 4.",
      "side": "back",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "output": "Gate 1"
        },
        {
          "module": "Logic",
          "input": "A"
        },
        {
          "module": "Euclid",
          "output": "Gate 2"
        },
        {
          "module": "Logic",
          "input": "B"
        },
        {
          "module": "Logic",
          "output": "And"
        },
        {
          "module": "Drums",
          "input": "Clap trig"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Euclid",
                "output": "Gate 1"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Logic",
                "input": "A"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Euclid",
                "output": "Gate 2"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Logic",
                "input": "B"
              }
            }
          },
          {
            "cable": {
              "from": {
                "module": "Logic",
                "output": "And"
              },
              "to": {
                "module": "Drums",
                "input": "Clap trig"
              }
            }
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Press Tab and shape the kit: turn KICK DECAY for a short thump or a long boom, and SNARE TONE from drum body to snare wires.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Drums",
          "param": "Kick decay"
        },
        {
          "module": "Drums",
          "param": "Snare tone"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "all": [
          {
            "param": {
              "module": "Drums",
              "param": "Kick decay"
            },
            "moved": 0.2
          },
          {
            "param": {
              "module": "Drums",
              "param": "Snare tone"
            },
            "moved": 0.2
          }
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "Turn SWING of the clock up a little. Every second sixteenth now comes a bit late and the groove starts to shuffle.",
      "side": "front",
      "highlight": [
        {
          "module": "Clock",
          "param": "Swing"
        }
      ],
      "done": {
        "param": {
          "module": "Clock",
          "param": "Swing"
        },
        "min": 56
      }
    },
    {
      "text": "A clock, a Euclidean sequencer, a bit of logic and a drum module make a whole beat. Try other numbers of steps and hits on tracks 3 and 4. Press Next to finish.",
      "done": {
        "next": true
      }
    }
  ]
}
